From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] keyboard: Keep a window moved for the OSK above it

When the keyboard comes up, _animateWindow unmaximizes the focus window
vertically and moves it to the top of the work area at the height left
above the keyboard. Mutter applies the unmaximize only once the client
acks it, and that restores the window's floating size and position,
centred in the work area: on the S10e the Yesman window came back 360
wide at x 36, and a chat's composer sat under the keys, out of reach.

Put the window back, full width from the top of the work area down to
the keyboard, whenever it moves or resizes while the keyboard is up.
Measure down to the keyboard's own top: the height above subtracts the
bottom panel, which on gnome-phone reserves no strut, so the last 18 px
of the window were still under the keys.

For gnome-shell-mobile 51.1.mobile.22 (/usr/src/gnome-mobile/gnome-shell
on the S10e, built into /opt/gnome-mobile by build51.sh).
---
--- a/js/ui/keyboard.js
+++ b/js/ui/keyboard.js
@@ -2356,11 +2356,31 @@
             window.unmaximize(Meta.MaximizeFlags.VERTICAL);
             window.move_resize_frame(false, frameRect.x, workArea.y, frameRect.width, workArea.height - (this.allocation.get_height() - (this._bottomPanelBox?.allocation.get_height() ?? 0)));
 
+            // Mutter applies the unmaximize only once the client acks it, and that restores the window's floating
+            // size and position, centred in the work area: the move above is lost and the window sits half under
+            // the keyboard. Put it back, full width from the top of the work area down to the keyboard, whenever
+            // it moves or resizes while the keyboard is up. Down to the keyboard's own top, not to the work area
+            // less the bottom panel as above: on gnome-phone that panel reserves no strut, so it is under the keys.
+            const fit = () => {
+                const rect = window.get_frame_rect();
+                const area = window.get_work_area_current_monitor();
+                const monitor = Main.layoutManager.keyboardMonitor;
+                const top = monitor.y + monitor.height - this.allocation.get_height();
+                const height = Math.min(area.y + area.height, top) - area.y;
+                if (rect.x !== area.x || rect.y !== area.y || rect.width !== area.width || rect.height !== height)
+                    window.move_resize_frame(false, area.x, area.y, area.width, height);
+            };
+            window.__keyboardFitIds = [window.connect('position-changed', fit), window.connect('size-changed', fit)];
+            fit();
+
             window.__keyboardMoved = true;
         } else if (!show && window.__keyboardMoved) {
             this.disconnect(this._bla);
             delete this._bla;
 
+            window.__keyboardFitIds.forEach(id => window.disconnect(id));
+            delete window.__keyboardFitIds;
+
             window.maximize(Meta.MaximizeFlags.VERTICAL);
             delete window.__keyboardMoved;
         }
